 "transcript": [
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "bosch 24 not draining, water sitting in bottom. help"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "Before you start, switch it off and unplug it. A Bosch dishwasher that won't drain usually has standing water because something is blocking the pump or the filter assembly, rather than a broken part. The most common cause is debris (like glass or food) caught in the filter or jammed against the small impeller inside the sump. Please take out the lower rack, twist and lift out the main cylindrical filter at the bottom of the tub, rinse it under the tap, and check the hole underneath for any blockages. Let me know if you found anything blocked there.\n[Helpful to see: image \"Where the filter is\" — The filter sits in the base of the dishwasher, usually under the bottom spray arm. Twist it out anticlockwise and rinse it under a tap. Typical layout — your dishwasher may differ.]"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "filter was clogged with food and a bit of broken glass. cleaned it, now drains ok and E:24 gone"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "That’s excellent news. It sounds like the broken glass and food debris were jamming the impeller in the sump, which is a very common cause of that E:24 error on Bosch models. To help prevent it happening again, try to scrape plates into the bin before loading them rather than rinsing heavy solids down the drain. If you need anything else or have any other questions about your appliance, just let me know."
  }
 ],
